<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Portsmouth, Rhode Island</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1638</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Portsmouth is a town on the northern part of Aquidneck Island in Rhode Island, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>. It was founded in 1638 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anne-hutchinson">Anne Hutchinson</a>, William Coddington and other religious dissenters exiled from Massachusetts, who signed the Portsmouth Compact. A split among the settlers led Coddington and his followers to found Newport in 1639.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/portsmouth-rhode-island.jpg" alt="Portsmouth, Rhode Island" width="320" height="179" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kenneth C. Zirkel · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portsmouth_Rhode_Island_Town_Hall.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
